#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059528 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "8369943c-d7d8-5b77-949b-b48a4a4a96d1" :question/math-academy-id "e-5780" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}}$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1-\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $1+\\textrm{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1+\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} \n&=\\dfrac {4 + \\textrm{i}} {1 - \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {1 + \\textrm{i}} {1 + \\textrm{i}}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {4 + 4\\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i} + \\textrm{i}^2} {1^2 - \\textrm{i}^2}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {4 + 5\\textrm{i} + (-1)} {1 - (-1)}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2}\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+\\textrm{i} b \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {3 + 5\\textrm{i}} {2} =\n\t\t\\dfrac{3} {2} + \\dfrac {5} {2} \\textrm{i}\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059529 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/id #uuid "107d76c0-349a-549d-adeb-f009492cd79c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5781" :question/problem "If $z_1 = -8-3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2\\textrm{i},$ then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $2\\textrm{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+2\\textrm{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-2\\textrm{i},$ or simply $-2\\textrm{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} \n&= \t\\dfrac {-8 - 3\\textrm{i}} {2\\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-2\\textrm{i}} {-2\\textrm{i}} \\[5pt]\n&= \t\\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6\\textrm{i}^2} {-4\\textrm{i}^2} \\[5pt]\n&= \t\\dfrac {16\\textrm{i} + 6(-1)} {-4(-1)} \\[5pt]\n&= \t\\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4}\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {-6 + 16\\textrm{i}} {4} &= - \\dfrac{6}{4} + \\dfrac{16}{4} \\textrm{i} \\[5pt]\n&=\t\t-\\dfrac{3} {2} + 4\\textrm{i}\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059530 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/id #uuid "74740363-2309-5680-9373-05ce0fed9bcf" :question/math-academy-id "e-6230" :question/problem "If $z_1=3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2 = 2+5\\textrm{i},$ then what is $z_1$ divided by $z_2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3\\textrm{i}}{2+5\\textrm i}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $2+5\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $2-5\\textrm{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $2-5\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5\\textrm{i}} \n&= \\dfrac {3 \\textrm{i}} {2 +5 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {2 -5 \\textrm{i}} {2-5\\textrm{i}}  \\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15 \\textrm{i}^2 } {2^2 - (5\\textrm{i})^2}  \\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15\\textrm{i}^2 } {4 - 25\\textrm{i}^2} \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} - 15(-1) } {4 - 25(-1)}  \\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15 } {29}\n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {6 \\textrm{i} + 15 } {29}=\n\t\t\\dfrac{15} {29} + \\dfrac {6} {29} \\textrm{i}\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059531 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/id #uuid "2fc036dd-7732-50ed-adef-8c37bd87fecd" :question/math-academy-id "e-6231" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{4}{-1+2\\textrm{i} }$ in the form $a+\\textrm{i}b.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-1+2\\textrm{i}$ and its conjugate is $-1-2\\textrm{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-1-2\\textrm{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {4} {-1 +2\\textrm{i}} \n&=\\dfrac {4} {-1 +2 \\textrm{i}} \\cdot \\dfrac {-1 -2 \\textrm{i}} {-1-2\\textrm{i}}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {(-1)^2 - (2\\textrm{i})^2}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {1 - 4\\textrm{i}^2}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {1 - 4(-1)}  \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {5} \n\t}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b \\textrm{i}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {-4 - 8 \\textrm{i} } {5} =\n\t\t-\\dfrac{4} {5} - \\dfrac {8} {5} \\textrm{i}\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21181676-9821-5fca-a4c7-cdbecac52c7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25}{73}-\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312575} {:answer/id #uuid "7e050e12-15ef-521c-9e98-aa24f5b5c83c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{73}{25}+\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312576} {:answer/id #uuid "081d7988-6036-5ed1-a0f7-26b830384945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{73}-\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312577} {:answer/id #uuid "f78a6cbf-308c-5344-9a3e-553549aec8d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{73}{25}-\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312578} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd81767-a04b-5381-81a1-848eab34480e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{73}+\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "081d7988-6036-5ed1-a0f7-26b830384945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{73}-\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312577} :answer-field/id #uuid "55766db4-24ff-57bf-a0a6-f2e5ad675fe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c6c84e8-7668-521a-a164-5f636d19f963" :question/math-academy-id "q-16431" :question/problem "if ${z}_{1}=5+5\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=-3+8\\text{i}$, then ${z}_{1}$ divided by ${z}_{2}$ equals" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5+5\\text{i}}{-3+8\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $-3+8\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-3-8\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3-8\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{5+5\\text{i}}{-3+8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+5\\text{i}}{-3+8\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3-8\\text{i}}{-3-8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-15-40\\text{i}-15\\text{i}-40{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-{8}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-15-55\\text{i}-40(-1)}{{3}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-15-55\\text{i}+40}{9+64} \\\\  & =\\frac{25-55\\text{i}}{73}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{25-55\\text{i}}{73}=\\frac{25}{73}-\\frac{55}{73}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7e8e09b-d9f2-53a8-9f1f-a6c34fc677ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312582} {:answer/id #uuid "f421e28e-4506-5d29-b26d-d312e88b94ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}+\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312583} {:answer/id #uuid "a343e7d9-cb8b-5f64-ab4e-8391a3d15ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{2}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312584} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac094ca-405d-5da2-a094-42adbba2b0cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312585} {:answer/id #uuid "d4fb8eef-e80a-581a-8a29-dd8e301b8064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{12}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4fb8eef-e80a-581a-8a29-dd8e301b8064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{12}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312586} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebddbc4b-84d6-5efe-896d-eba96a7a5e01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ff7ffb7-e3d5-54df-983e-2a539ba75182" :question/math-academy-id "q-167671" :question/problem "$\\frac{5-2\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-2\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5-2\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-2\\text{i}}{1-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-10\\text{i}-2\\text{i}+4{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{2}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-12\\text{i}+4(-1)}{1-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-12\\text{i}-4}{1+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{5}=\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{12}{5}\\text{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bee40c07-4dc5-5c21-8bb9-c48b098e4538" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{3}{10}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312589} {:answer/id #uuid "36af84d1-4727-5a19-a086-57d2befa239d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}-\\frac{2}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312590} {:answer/id #uuid "63f1e044-ab50-56cc-8347-c933894aa714" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{3}{8}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312591} {:answer/id #uuid "01863964-8869-5dcd-9b5f-e90a7fe7405e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{4}{5}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312592} {:answer/id #uuid "f11d785f-a32b-50f9-bfe3-3662de6b1113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f11d785f-a32b-50f9-bfe3-3662de6b1113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312593} :answer-field/id #uuid "92741674-11d2-58e5-a2f2-f54029443ff3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ada4b0f-8d44-546b-8352-178ace59db0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-167673" :question/problem "$\\frac{4\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $3-\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3+\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3+\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}} & =\\frac{4\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3+\\text{i}}{3+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\text{i}(3+\\text{i})}{{3}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+4{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+4(-1)}{9+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+12\\text{i}}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4+12\\text{i}}{10} & =-\\frac{4}{10}+\\frac{12}{10}\\text{i} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "084a5f6e-3881-53f1-90f5-6a65a168ce55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312596} {:answer/id #uuid "57d41e20-d8fe-5176-a520-922edf91372f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}+2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312597} {:answer/id #uuid "57c1c406-2e15-5e3d-8750-9315e5f8f88d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{2}{9}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312598} {:answer/id #uuid "a4966510-e88a-5700-87ed-663bb022eb83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}-2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312599} {:answer/id #uuid "d53d6f75-887d-547c-86ca-d8eb886b12bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4966510-e88a-5700-87ed-663bb022eb83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}-2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312599} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0d9bd20-96ee-5744-b296-f53a156df837" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f7f340b-160f-5ff4-a53d-52f410581d8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-167676" :question/problem "$\\frac{6-4\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $3\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+3\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-3\\text{i},$ or simply $-3\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6-4\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{6-4\\text{i}}{3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3\\text{i}}{-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18\\text{i}+12{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18\\text{i}+12(-1)}{-9(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12-18\\text{i}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-12-18\\text{i}}{9} & =-\\frac{12}{9}-\\frac{18}{9}\\text{i} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dccdf72c-3779-5a46-a74e-92b967360df5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312603} {:answer/id #uuid "e586f5ec-00a0-5b8f-bca7-5733d5ee2832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e586f5ec-00a0-5b8f-bca7-5733d5ee2832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312604} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c706a72-b105-5a8f-861f-7c2794bcfe2f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312602} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ec873c9-23d3-58b5-8323-77f256645aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ec873c9-23d3-58b5-8323-77f256645aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312606} :answer-field/id #uuid "eee10c9a-70cb-5cc6-9585-6e3383379ff9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "476d5ed3-04f5-5a62-90e6-9af09a1395e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-275375" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-4}{2-6\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $2-6\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $2+6\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $2+6\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4}{2-6\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-4}{2-6\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{2+6\\text{i}}{2+6\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{4+12\\text{i}-12\\text{i}-36{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{4-36{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{4-(36)(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{4+36} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{40}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8-24\\text{i}}{40}=-\\frac{8}{40}-\\frac{24}{40}\\text{i}=(-\\frac{1}{5})+(-\\frac{3}{5})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6c51f5e-9ea1-5090-b338-c69782947ed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{61}{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6c51f5e-9ea1-5090-b338-c69782947ed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{61}{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312609} :answer-field/id #uuid "1160c31f-010b-51da-8482-5c4ac67318e0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312608} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df7951f5-b418-52aa-8fcf-1d31709708f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df7951f5-b418-52aa-8fcf-1d31709708f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312611} :answer-field/id #uuid "d792d74a-f591-5bbd-a83d-135f0127fa08" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312610}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6645a6eb-e0b8-5183-8e27-1ebca6dc4649" :question/math-academy-id "q-316756" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{12-19\\text{i}}{8-11\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $8-11\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $8+11\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $8+11\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12-19\\text{i}}{8-11\\text{i}} & =\\frac{12-19\\text{i}}{8-11\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{8+11\\text{i}}{8+11\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(12-19\\text{i})(8+11\\text{i})}{(8-11\\text{i})(8+11\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{96+132\\text{i}-152\\text{i}-209{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{8}^{2}-(11\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{96-20\\text{i}-209(-1)}{{8}^{2}+{11}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{96-20\\text{i}+209}{64+121} \\\\  & =\\frac{305-20\\text{i}}{185} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(61-4\\text{i})}{5\\cdot 37} \\\\  & =\\frac{61-4\\text{i}}{37}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{61-4\\text{i}}{37}=(\\frac{61}{37})+(-\\frac{4}{37})\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1de0b10b-47fe-56b5-b937-b5569e5e9101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1de0b10b-47fe-56b5-b937-b5569e5e9101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275630} :answer-field/id #uuid "764ff62d-2f8e-5ef3-af41-de7e5875e934" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275629} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c0eb84b-6c92-5b7e-a069-18784297930a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c0eb84b-6c92-5b7e-a069-18784297930a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275632} :answer-field/id #uuid "c07b9bab-4835-5fbd-a748-3f03e4df9125" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8165711-54b7-5043-aeb6-860843b30537" :question/math-academy-id "q-316847" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-3\\text{i}}{1-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}-15{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}-15(-1)}{1-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\text{i}+15}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{15+5\\text{i}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{15+5\\text{i}}{10}=(\\frac{3}{2})+(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{i}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc6c30d1-8ecf-50e6-a66a-0909c2b8f0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265139} {:answer/id #uuid "e4087cb9-6485-532d-a03a-6bccbef0a9d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc6c30d1-8ecf-50e6-a66a-0909c2b8f0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265139} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6ada72-28bf-5950-a297-c0f517d035b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f5fc1cf-968d-5714-a780-e00c0a91b6cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f5fc1cf-968d-5714-a780-e00c0a91b6cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265141} :answer-field/id #uuid "86bdf9c3-c1fb-5167-946d-240bbabbd436" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e535981f-647e-56d4-8c1b-fdc761659fc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316848" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $3-\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3+\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3+\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}} & =\\frac{7\\text{i}}{3-\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3+\\text{i}}{3+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21\\text{i}+7{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21\\text{i}+7(-1)}{9-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7+21\\text{i}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-7+21\\text{i}}{10}=(-\\frac{7}{10})+(\\frac{21}{10})\\,\\text{i}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50ef3393-d193-5938-a98f-61e8b6252185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312615} {:answer/id #uuid "142e53ac-9713-5f68-8675-2fd5c2f6299e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50ef3393-d193-5938-a98f-61e8b6252185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312615} :answer-field/id #uuid "9805af53-153b-5946-8eed-12848701eddc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4107bcb7-5471-52e6-b6b4-106d1dd6fb9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4107bcb7-5471-52e6-b6b4-106d1dd6fb9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312618} :answer-field/id #uuid "5502af53-5b6f-57c4-acd0-9a1bce208373" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312617}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2fcaadd-b7ff-5b19-b396-85cf3b042495" :question/math-academy-id "q-316851" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}}=($\n {{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-2+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2-3\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10\\text{i}-15{\\text{i}}^{2}}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10\\text{i}-15(-1)}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{15-10\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{15-10\\text{i}}{13}=(\\frac{15}{13})+(-\\frac{10}{13})\\,\\text{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312619 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "154c6c99-1a73-5bc5-b2dc-394a4b3bddc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312621} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a1987a-e8e8-5973-a87c-206ecd3b54fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5a1987a-e8e8-5973-a87c-206ecd3b54fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 