owledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43b52200-9269-5ea7-beb6-272c1721daae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43b52200-9269-5ea7-beb6-272c1721daae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312627} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f4fa94e-0332-59f4-8a4d-3dd24e907dae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312626} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2169ea74-a372-5c4b-8838-f967e2b52338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2169ea74-a372-5c4b-8838-f967e2b52338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312629} :answer-field/id #uuid "f994d418-900c-5adb-a627-171c2efb5cf7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5915603-e652-5ba7-a613-b88aecd96c3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316872" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5}{-2+3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-2+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{-2+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5}{-2+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2-3\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(-2-3\\text{i})}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-15\\text{i}}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-15\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-10-15\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{10}{13})+(-\\frac{15}{13})\\,\\text{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb4bc66f-5ae0-5f58-a1e6-a9582186c253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312632} {:answer/id #uuid "1e2a34c0-1ac1-5140-a670-d310b4a3ba4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e2a34c0-1ac1-5140-a670-d310b4a3ba4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312633} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ebef65-aece-5350-a453-99badfd1fe77" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312631} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42066600-9df5-5a91-808a-1517bd3923ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42066600-9df5-5a91-808a-1517bd3923ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312635} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8c0b29c-a4c9-579a-a525-4e18cab1c0ba" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62c0981c-dc22-5dd8-9db1-93ade390bfe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-316886" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-12+5\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $4\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+4\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-4\\text{i},$ or simply $-4\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-12+5\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-12+5\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-4\\text{i}}{-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{48\\text{i}-20{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{48\\text{i}-20(-1)}{-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{20+48\\text{i}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20+48\\text{i}}{16} & =\\frac{20}{16}+\\frac{48}{16}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{4})+(3)\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "477fbecb-e5a4-5569-8eea-8ce894cd68c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "477fbecb-e5a4-5569-8eea-8ce894cd68c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312638} :answer-field/id #uuid "29008319-9cf4-50b5-b3b0-892033bd0dfe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "272244b3-8eba-577b-b934-35edb47685b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "272244b3-8eba-577b-b934-35edb47685b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312640} :answer-field/id #uuid "5842e02f-2e2b-567d-981f-2d4c60c02eaf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77aba267-0ace-52cd-b48c-fb373812d066" :question/math-academy-id "q-316888" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $2\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+2\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-2\\text{i},$ or simply $-2\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-6-7\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2\\text{i}}{-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+14{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+14(-1)}{-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14+12\\text{i}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-14+12\\text{i}}{4} & =-\\frac{14}{4}+\\frac{12}{4}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{7}{2})+(3)\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6def0763-0118-5b51-9c8d-aab0ebc7a1f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6def0763-0118-5b51-9c8d-aab0ebc7a1f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312643} :answer-field/id #uuid "e13f8ccf-eab4-57e7-b21f-5c959ecb417c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312642} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90ec2cd9-0932-58d4-9c41-4ca9408e9a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90ec2cd9-0932-58d4-9c41-4ca9408e9a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312645} :answer-field/id #uuid "27657b89-78a5-5728-a415-4e0c075ac551" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d55d864-b6fe-5c73-b70e-93372f20943b" :question/math-academy-id "q-316891" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-5-9\\text{i}}{10\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $10\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+10\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-10\\text{i},$ or simply $-10\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-10\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-5-9\\text{i}}{10\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-5-9\\text{i}}{10\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-10\\text{i}}{-10\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{50\\text{i}+90{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-100{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{50\\text{i}+90(-1)}{-100(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-90+50\\text{i}}{100}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-90+50\\text{i}}{100} & =-\\frac{90}{100}+\\frac{50}{100}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{9}{10})+(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c37ba39-e719-5983-9ff5-f6447f7e974e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265181} {:answer/id #uuid "69274d97-1df3-54e5-a65e-c988603ba447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c37ba39-e719-5983-9ff5-f6447f7e974e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265181} :answer-field/id #uuid "095e16a8-3a79-5cc1-b77c-c18462414596" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bdc5b66-6608-56d4-bd89-df374350f4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bdc5b66-6608-56d4-bd89-df374350f4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265184} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed86f562-7f92-581c-8aba-9ee39c907bd9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1599423c-9248-5ffa-9d17-823c2bf2328f" :question/math-academy-id "q-316904" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-2-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2+3\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(5+2\\text{i})(-2+3\\text{i})}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+15\\text{i}-4\\text{i}+6{\\text{i}}^{2}}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10+11\\text{i}+6(-1)}{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{-16+11\\text{i}}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-16+11\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{16}{13})+(\\frac{11}{13})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bea7014a-2ec7-5bc1-9286-c1ed2aadf3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{13}-\\frac{27}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265208} {:answer/id #uuid "917b6f05-edd5-53dc-8a8e-3a94bc2e3f1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{13}+\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265209} {:answer/id #uuid "25ea1f31-37a2-55c3-8cca-9c788a9e0c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{13}+\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265210} {:answer/id #uuid "25e30022-e454-5b13-933e-a1a0a68b584c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265211} {:answer/id #uuid "50a4f5be-7f4f-5da6-b15b-e24fe8e99cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50a4f5be-7f4f-5da6-b15b-e24fe8e99cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265212} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfdf262a-8a69-5f89-9cb7-40b82cfbac0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ca3346d-d2b9-53ea-9f84-d9305b392ee5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74648" :question/problem "$\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $-3+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-3-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-3-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{9}{-3+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-3-2\\text{i}}{-3-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9+6\\text{i}-6\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9-4(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-27-18\\text{i}}{13}=-\\frac{27}{13}-\\frac{18}{13}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "678ba6cb-b259-5a25-858c-9db161a34ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Real Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcb66cc9-310b-52db-911a-02b01a483346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}+\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312648} {:answer/id #uuid "7b107270-0473-5d03-996c-502821c6dcb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}-\\frac{8}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312649} {:answer/id #uuid "2b46f602-afec-5743-9fc8-b77bdeb32b3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}+\\frac{3}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312650} {:answer/id #uuid "383b8013-c311-5906-9ac8-c50b6d26c49f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312651} {:answer/id #uuid "f9346a76-0b1f-571a-a5a2-63a0a1cfa96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcb66cc9-310b-52db-911a-02b01a483346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}+\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312648} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef72d2f-c869-50d2-b7b3-fe2ba8ee29bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312647}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca9f1789-91be-5c8b-acf7-fb31d20e253d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74649" :question/problem "$\\frac{-10}{4+3\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $4+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $4-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $4-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-10}{4+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-10}{4+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{4-3\\text{i}}{4-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{16-12\\text{i}+12\\text{i}-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{16-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{16-(9)(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{16+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{25}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-40+30\\text{i}}{25}=-\\frac{40}{25}+\\frac{30}{25}\\text{i}=-\\frac{8}{5}+\\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Complex Number by an Imaginary Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3ae78aa-a8ba-5371-9a04-15acfd48b66f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265215} {:answer/id #uuid "15b6bed4-902c-5c4e-becf-c810855b2013" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265216} {:answer/id #uuid "b3423c26-80ab-5b46-b4b5-59bfd96f259c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265217} {:answer/id #uuid "c4eabb36-f6b3-577e-9d33-49b95f12f027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265218} {:answer/id #uuid "f147c615-f613-5bfb-ac8f-6df935875467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3423c26-80ab-5b46-b4b5-59bfd96f259c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265217} :answer-field/id #uuid "e48681cf-2d37-5061-9ef2-e8325e724d7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b1df748-6885-5736-937a-15d2623e818b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74659" :question/problem "If ${z}_{1}=1-12\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=8\\text{i}$, then ${z}_{1}$ divided by ${z}_{2}$ equals" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $8\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+8\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-8\\text{i},$ or simply $-8\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-8\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-12\\text{i}}{8\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-8\\text{i}}{-8\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+96{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-64{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+96(-1)}{-64(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-96-8\\text{i}}{64}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-96-8\\text{i}}{64}=-\\frac{96}{64}-\\frac{8}{64}\\text{i}=-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27da4eb7-48c8-58f4-9676-c88d659f5fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing an Imaginary Number by a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9eba4f7-b1d0-50e9-be98-00ba1aea8352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059204} {:answer/id #uuid "11f70417-93a3-55e4-a3be-2fa2e96d5c26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{3}{2}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059205} {:answer/id #uuid "2884a1ba-ffba-56a3-8ab5-f970246b15dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 + 3\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059206} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff0c628-d0de-5903-8999-0ab70f1fdaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{3}{2}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059207} {:answer/id #uuid "7e229f67-6464-5089-af2f-0b2da0e6b904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 - 3\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ff0c628-d0de-5903-8999-0ab70f1fdaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{3}{2}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059207} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf4dec5c-b82c-5c00-8bcf-aa31113066b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059203}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed8906fc-614a-57ed-9859-dffede544532" :question/math-academy-id "q-963" :question/problem "$\\frac{3\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator is $1+\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1-\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1-\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}} & =\\frac{3\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1-\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\text{i}-3{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\text{i}-3(-1)}{1-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\text{i}+3}{1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\text{i}+3}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\text{i}+3}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d7a092-1997-5305-b44c-47c41bc9ac57" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Two Complex Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df66d735-f8eb-5fad-b868-b26150986e2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15} - \\frac{4}{5}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059210} {:answer/id #uuid "32c2a184-cac9-5847-a40b-f9989b4fd3b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5} - \\frac{4}{5}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059211} {:answer/id #uuid "3902d287-8e83-52a1-8156-d3e55c8e0dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{4}{5}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059212} {:answer/id #uuid "4cdc7ce5-c1ba-56e2-b129-b62bf83b2047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5} - \\frac{8}{15}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059213} {:answer/id #uuid "774acff5-ab15-54e8-b290-c12c58e14f68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{8}{15}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df66d735-f8eb-5fad-b868-b26150986e2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15} - \\frac{4}{5}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059210} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e39936c-7a2c-5bd2-9d87-42450a867651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b600cc8-09de-5ea0-a5bb-76d034792338" :question/math-academy-id "q-964" :question/problem "If ${z}_{1}=2-5\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=6+3\\text{i}$, then ${z}_{1}$ divided by ${z}_{2}$ equals" :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-5\\text{i}}{6+3\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is $6+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $6-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $6-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{2-5\\text{i}}{6+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-5\\text{i}}{6+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{6-3\\text{i}}{6-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-6\\text{i}-30\\text{i}+15{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{6}^{2}-{3}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-36\\text{i}+15(-1)}{{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-36\\text{i}-15}{36+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-36\\text{i}}{45}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3-36\\text{i}}{45}=-\\frac{3}{45}-\\frac{36}{45}\\text{i}=-\\frac{1}{15}-\\frac{4}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
